---
description: Never git push (or push tags) without explicit user approval
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git push requires approval

Do **not** run any command that publishes to a remote unless the user explicitly asks in
that conversation turn. This includes:

- `git push` (any branch, with or without `-u`)
- `git push origin --tags` / pushing individual tags
- `gh` commands that publish (e.g. `gh pr create` is OK when asked; pushing is not)

Allowed without a separate push request:

- Local git: `status`, `diff`, `log`, `fetch`, `commit` (only when user asked to commit)
- Creating tags **locally** when it helps the task
- CI/workflow YAML that pushes on GitHub Actions (not the agent shell)

After local commits or tags, **stop** and tell the user what is ready to push; wait for
approval. Do not push "to finish the task" or because CI expects it on the remote.

Exception: user says "push", "push to origin", "publish the tag", etc. in the same request.
